## Address Task 3 review findings for the staged owl-generator orchestration

Context: Fixes five review findings against the task-3 commit (`3ff760a2`)
for the `staged-ontology-generate` plan. No API/UI/session-orchestration
code touched; the deprecated one-shot bridge (`engine.py`) removal stays
scoped to Task 4 as before. Followed strict TDD: each finding got a
focused failing test, an observed RED, then the minimal fix to GREEN.

Changes:

1. tests/eval/staged_contract.py — **(Important)** detection-tagged
   constraint checks now exercise the real `staged.detect_entities()`
   orchestrator instead of calling `schemas.parse_detection_payload()`
   directly with a hand-written literal. New `_run_detection_for_example()`
   builds existing anchors / metadata / selected docs from each dataset
   row's own `input` (`existing_ontology`/`metadata`/`corpus`), scripts two
   `staged.call_serving_endpoint` responses (a `get_metadata` tool-call
   round-trip dispatched for real through `dispatch_tool`/`TOOL_HANDLERS` —
   offline-safe, no network — followed by the final structured answer, its
   candidates built by `_build_scripted_detection_payload()` from the row's
   own constraints), and asserts the observed `trace_name`. Rewrote
   `_c_all_included`, `_c_excludes_anchor`, `_c_excludes_anchor_alt`,
   `_c_min_new_candidates`, `_c_synonyms_as_alt`, and `_c_no_separate_synonym`
   to call it. `_c_does_not_parse` now branches on the row's own
   `input.stage`: for a `detect` row it inspects the tool definitions
   actually offered to the scripted LLM call (`mock_llm.call_args_list[...]
   .kwargs["tools"]`) and the tool calls actually dispatched
   (`DetectionResult.steps`) for `ai_parse_document`/`check_owl_pitfalls`,
   rather than a static `TOOL_DEFINITIONS` name check that would pass even
   if a bug caused one to be dispatched anyway; for the one completion-stage
   row it delegates to `_c_no_document_tools` (real `infer_attributes()`
   call, `tools=None`). The deterministic/offline eval and the pre-existing
   parsed-corpus gate are unaffected — only `call_serving_endpoint` is
   scripted, still no live endpoint.
2. src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py — per-tool MLflow tracing for
   Stage-1 tool dispatch. Added `_dispatch_detection_tool()`, a local
   `@trace_tool()`-wrapped wrapper around the existing `dispatch_tool()`
   call in `detect_entities()`'s tool loop. `dispatch_tool` itself (shared
   by ~10 other agent engines' ReAct loops) and the shared tool handlers
   are untouched — adding a span inside the shared helper would have
   changed every one of those agents' traces, which is out of scope here.
   `trace_tool`'s existing per-handler pattern (statically decorating one
   handler, e.g. `agent_graph_interpreter.tools.tool_get_entity_details`)
   doesn't fit a tool name chosen dynamically per LLM tool call, so this is
   a thin local dispatcher instead; its positional call signature
   `(ctx, tool_name, arguments)` matches `trace_tool`'s existing
   argument-index contract exactly, so no change was needed there either.
3. src/agents/tracing.py — `trace_tool()` span outputs now include a
   `status` (`"ok"`/`"error"`) alongside the existing `result_length`,
   derived from whether the JSON result string carries a top-level `error`
   key (`_tool_result_status()`, new) — so a tool call's name (already a
   span input) and outcome are both visible on the trace. Purely additive;
   the wrapped function's return value is unchanged (no handler behaviour
   change).
4. src/agents/tracing.py — terminology fix. `trace_agent()`'s local `tags`
   variable renamed to `attributes` (it is passed to `Span.set_attributes`,
   never a trace-tags API), and its docstring — plus the corresponding
   passage in SPEC.md §8 — corrected from "trace tags/attributes" to
   "span attributes … not MLflow trace-level tags (`mlflow.set_trace_tag`
   / trace `tags=`), which this module does not use." No behaviour change;
   this repo has no existing use of the real trace-tags API, so none was
   added (avoiding overreach).
