## Fix live Stage-1 false rejection when every selected entity is already a locked anchor

Context: Two live Generate tasks (`aa2f34cc`, `72fd9955`) failed after a
successful Foundation Model call with `output is not valid JSON: Expecting
value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)`; the draft stayed `null`. Root cause: the
active session's 10 selected tables' core entities were ALL already among
its 15 locked ontology anchors, so the model had no genuinely NEW grounded
candidate — the Stage-1 prompt said "JSON only" but never defined what to
answer in that case, so the model wrote prose/analysis instead of
`{"candidate_entities": []}`, and `detect_entities` correctly-but-
unhelpfully rejected the malformed output. Fixed per strict TDD and the AI
Feature Lifecycle gate, prompt-only (no rewrite/re-prompt loop; reject-only
architecture unchanged).

Changes:

1. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py`
   `build_detection_system_prompt` now states, immediately after the
   anchors listing, that existing anchors are context-not-candidates and
   that when nothing new is grounded the mandatory answer is exactly
   `{"candidate_entities": []}` (no explanation/refusal/prose/fence). The
   OUTPUT section additionally requires the first character of the reply
   to be `{` and forbids an analysis/reasoning preamble before the JSON —
   added after live reproduction showed the model narrating visible
   reasoning ahead of its JSON answer.
2. `src/back/objects/ontology/GenerateWorkflow.py`
   `run_detection`'s rejection path no longer echoes the raw parser/schema
   exception text to the user; it raises a generic `DraftValidationError`
   stating the model failed the structured contract and suggesting a
   retry. The raw detail is still logged server-side for debugging.
3. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_staged.py`
   Added `TestZeroCandidateContract` (5 tests pinning the exact empty-JSON
   contract wording, anchors-are-context wording, no-prose/refusal
   wording, contract stated even with zero anchors, and the no-reasoning-
   preamble/first-char-`{` rule) and
   `test_empty_candidate_list_is_a_successful_result_not_a_rejection`
   (confirms `detect_entities` treats an empty candidate list as a
   successful, non-rejected result).
4. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_schemas.py`
   Added 2 tests pinning that `parse_detection_payload` already accepted
   — and continues to accept — an empty `candidate_entities` list, with
   and without existing anchors.
5. `tests/units/ontology/test_generate_workflow.py`
   Added `test_detection_rejection_message_is_generic_not_raw_parser_text`
   pinning that the user-facing rejection message never leaks the raw
   parser exception text.
6. `tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl` and
   `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl` (byte-
   identical mirrors)
   Added regression row `staged-zero-new-candidates-001`: 2 tables, both
   already covered by 2 locked anchors, expecting
   `success=True`/`rejected=False`/`candidate_entities=[]`.
7. `tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py`
   Raised `_MIN_STAGED_EXAMPLES` from 14 to 15; added
