## Implement transport-level structured output for Stage-1 detection (supersedes the prompt-only fix above)

Context: the prompt-only zero-new-candidate fix above was reported
insufficient by explicit user feedback — the exact-case reproduction
against the user's own active endpoint
(`benoit_cayla.ontobricks-todrop.monclaudesonnetamoi`) only succeeded on 1
of 5 calls, with the model narrating a visible reasoning preamble before
its JSON on the other 4 despite the strengthened "first character must be
`{`" instruction. The user independently confirmed by directly probing
that endpoint: (1) `response_format={"type":"json_object"}` returns 400
unsupported; (2) `response_format={"type":"json_schema","json_schema":
{...}}` is accepted and returns exactly the schema-shaped JSON; (3)
combining `response_format` with `tools` in the same request is rejected
("Cannot specify both response_format and tools"). Fixed per strict TDD:
`detect_entities` is now a bounded tool-gathering phase followed by
exactly one schema-enforced finalization call, with the answer shape
enforced at the transport layer, not only requested in the prompt. No
rewrite/re-prompt loop added; reject-only architecture unchanged.

Changes:

1. `src/shared/llm_target.py`
   `build_llm_request` gained an optional `response_format` parameter
   (defaults to `None` — every other caller's payload is byte-identical).
   Combining `tools` and `response_format` now raises `ValueError`
   fail-fast, client-side, before any network call — the endpoint contract
   rejects that combination.
2. `src/agents/engine_base.py`
   `call_serving_endpoint` gained the same optional `response_format`
   pass-through. An endpoint that rejects `response_format` with a clear
   400 (the same "does not support the ... parameter" shape already
   handled for `temperature`) has it stripped and the request retried
   once, with the ban cached per endpoint for later calls — mirrors the
   pre-existing `temperature` ban-cache mechanism exactly; no new caching
   structure needed.
3. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py`
   Added `DETECTION_RESPONSE_FORMAT` — a strict
   `{"type": "json_schema", ..., "strict": true}` constant whose item
   schema mirrors `parse_detection_payload`'s own field contract exactly
   (`canonical_label`, `description`, `type_hint` (enum `["class"]`),
   `evidence` (`source`/`excerpt`), `alternate_labels`); every object
   `additionalProperties: false` and every field `required`.
4. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py`
   `detect_entities` refactored into two phases: a bounded tool-GATHERING
   loop (`tools=` the metadata/document tools, never `response_format`;
   renamed budget constant `_MAX_DETECTION_ITERATIONS` ->
   `_MAX_GATHERING_ITERATIONS`) followed by exactly ONE schema-enforced
   FINALIZATION call (`tools=None`,
   `response_format=schemas.DETECTION_RESPONSE_FORMAT`). A gathering turn
   with no tool calls ends gathering; its content is discarded — never
   parsed as the answer, and not even carried into the finalization
   conversation. If the endpoint rejects `tools` outright (400/422),
   gathering is skipped entirely and finalization is called directly. The
   old "truncated -> ask the model to re-emit concisely" retry was removed
   along with the single-phase loop it belonged to: a length-truncated
   finalization answer now fails clearly, with no re-prompt.
5. `tests/units/shared/test_llm_target.py`
   3 new tests: `response_format` included when provided, absent by
   default, `ValueError` raised when combined with `tools`.
6. `tests/units/agents/test_agent_engine_base.py`
   6 new tests: `response_format` included/absent, `ValueError` raised
   with zero network calls when combined with `tools`, unsupported
   `response_format` stripped-and-retried-once, the ban cached across
   calls to the same endpoint.
7. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_schemas.py`
   Added `TestDetectionResponseFormat` (4 tests: is a `json_schema`
   response_format with `strict: true`; requires `candidate_entities` as
   an array with `additionalProperties: false`; the item schema's
   properties/required/enum/`additionalProperties` match the parser's own
   field contract exactly; an empty-list answer still parses cleanly).
8. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_staged.py`
   Added `TestTwoPhaseDetectionArchitecture` (6 tests: tools and
   response_format are never sent in the same call; gathering calls never
   carry response_format; the finalization call always carries the strict
   schema with `tools=None`; a gather-stop turn's prose is ignored and not
   carried into the finalization conversation; finalization receives the
   accumulated tool call/result context; a bounded gathering budget still
   reaches finalization) and `TestDetectionResponseFormatFallbackIntegration`
   (1 end-to-end test: a real `detect_entities` call through the real,
   only-HTTP-mocked `call_serving_endpoint` still succeeds when the
   endpoint rejects `response_format`). Every existing `TestDetectEntities`
   test updated for the new two-call-minimum shape (a gathering turn now
   always precedes the finalization answer that is actually parsed); added
   `test_finalization_truncation_fails_without_reprompt` and
   `test_gathering_truncation_is_treated_as_a_gather_stop` to pin the
   no-re-prompt truncation contract explicitly; two pre-existing
   `TestPerToolTracing` scripts extended with the extra gather-stop
   response the new architecture requires.
9. `tests/eval/staged_contract.py`
   `_run_detection_for_example`'s scripted flow updated from 2 to 3
   responses (tool call, gather-stop, finalization) to match the new
   two-phase shape.
10. `tests/eval/test_run_agent_owl_generator.py`
    `test_does_not_cost_an_extra_live_call_per_row`'s
    `spy_llm.call_count` assertion updated `6` -> `11` (each
    `detect_entities()` call is now 2 LLM round-trips, not 1: 5 detect
    rows * 2 + 1 completion-chain call).
11. `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md`
    Added the "Transport-level structured output" bullet to §3a; added the
